# netsurf: Vita hardware-test diagnostics, round 2 (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# Hardware run 1 (doc 10 §Results): every page stayed "load not finished"
# with no document, while the same code loads in the host simulator. This
# round makes the next run conclusive and carries the likely fix:
# - engine log: NetSurf's NSLOG (all levels) and MacSurf's
#   macsurf_debug_log_writef() traces to ux0:data/VitaBrowser/netsurf.log,
#   buffered, flushed each second, capped at 16 MB;
# - scheduler counters (added / fired / pending) and a once-a-second
#   load-status line per page until its document arrives (NEW_CONTENT);
# - window events, status text and URL changes logged;
# - stall rescue: a page with no document 1.5 s after navigating switches
#   on MacSurf's fetch_pump() (content/fetch.c fixes90) every loop
#   iteration, and the log says so per page;
# - the HUD / message overlay repaints on its own (it stayed stale on L/R
#   while pages had no document).
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md.

